{"id":"s2.1.11","slug":"fluid-weight-conversions","title":"Fluid and Weight Conversions","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">It is recommended to memorize all common fluid and weight conversions, even those that can be derived, to save time.</p><ul class=\"list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-4\"><li>1 gallon = 4 quarts = 16 cups = 128 oz = 231 in³</li><li>1 quart = 2 pints</li><li>1 pint = 2 cups</li><li>1 cup = 8 oz</li><li>1 tbsp = 0.5 oz</li><li>1 tsp = 1/6 oz</li><li>1 pound = 16 oz</li><li>1 ton = 2000 lbs</li></ul>","summary":"It is recommended to memorize all common fluid and weight conversions, even those that can be derived, to save time.","generation_guideline":"Generate a problem that requires converting between different units of fluid volume or weight.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"1 quart = ___ cups","answer":"4","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":2,"text":"1 quart = ___ ounces","answer":"32","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":3,"text":"3 pints = ___ ounces","answer":"48","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":4,"text":"3 gallons = ___ cubic inches","answer":"693","kind":"exact","tags":["conversions"]},{"id":5,"text":"$\\frac{2}{3}$ gallon = ___ cubic inches","answer":"154","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","conversions"]},{"id":6,"text":"$1\\frac{1}{3}$ gallon = ___ cubic inches","answer":"308","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","conversions"]},{"id":7,"text":"75% of 1 gallon = ___ ounces","answer":"96","kind":"exact","tags":["percent"]},{"id":8,"text":"256 ounces = ___ pounds","answer":"16","kind":"exact","tags":["conversions"]},{"id":9,"text":"750 pounds = ___ % of a ton","answer":"37.5%","kind":"exact","tags":["percent","conversions"]},{"id":10,"text":"75% of a gallon = ___ pints","answer":"6","kind":"exact","tags":["percent"]},{"id":11,"text":"$12\\frac{1}{2}\\%$ of a pint = ___ ounces","answer":"2","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","percent"]},{"id":12,"text":"4 pints is what % of a gallon:","answer":"50%","kind":"exact","tags":["percent"]},{"id":13,"text":"2 quarts is what % of a pint:","answer":"400%","kind":"exact","tags":["percent"]},{"id":14,"text":"6 tablespoons is ___ % of a cup","answer":"37.5%","kind":"exact","tags":["percent"]},{"id":15,"text":"9 cups is what % of a quart:","answer":"225%","kind":"exact","tags":["percent"]},{"id":16,"text":"A quart is what % of a cup:","answer":"400%","kind":"exact","tags":["percent"]},{"id":17,"text":"2541 cubic inches = ___ gallons","answer":"11","kind":"exact","tags":["conversions"]},{"id":18,"text":"3 pints is what % of a cup:","answer":"600%","kind":"exact","tags":["percent"]},{"id":19,"text":"3 pints is what % of a gallon:","answer":"37.5%","kind":"exact","tags":["percent"]},{"id":20,"text":"5 gallons = ___ cubic inches","answer":"1155","kind":"exact","tags":["conversions"]},{"id":21,"text":"32 ounces = ___ pints","answer":"2","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":22,"text":"3.5 pints = ___ quarts","answer":"1.75","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":23,"text":"2.5 pints = ___ cups","answer":"5","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":24,"text":"37.5% of a gallon is ___ pints","answer":"3","kind":"exact","tags":["percent"]},{"id":25,"text":"62.5% of a gallon is ___ quarts","answer":"2.5","kind":"exact","tags":["percent"]},{"id":26,"text":"87.5% of a gallon is ___ ounces","answer":"112","kind":"exact","tags":["percent"]},{"id":27,"text":"16 ounces is what part of a gallon:","answer":"1/8","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":28,"text":"1 gallon = ___ cubic inches","answer":"231","kind":"exact","tags":["conversions"]},{"id":29,"text":"$\\frac{3}{11}$ of a gallon = ___ cubic inches","answer":"63","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","conversions"]},{"id":30,"text":"$\\frac{3}{8}$ of a quart = ___ ounces","answer":"12","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions"]},{"id":31,"text":"$\\frac{7}{11}$ of a gallon = ___ cubic inches","answer":"147","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","conversions"]},{"id":32,"text":"3 quarts and 2 pints = ___ oun